# Files that are present in this folder but must never be served.
#
# `website/` is edited and `website/` is published, so this list is the only
# boundary between a working file and a public URL. Cloudflare's asset uploader
# reads it (gitignore syntax); the local dev server does not, which is why
# `just website` can still serve everything here at `/` — including
# `tools/ink-probe.html`, which needs to be same-origin with `index.html` to
# measure it in a frame.
#
# Exact paths and directory entries only, deliberately: a glob like
# `/assets/img/*` would also drop `terrain-matte.png`, `og.png`, and
# `speckle.svg`, which DO ship. `website/tools/published-tree.py` asserts the
# resulting tree against an expected set and is what makes this list safe to
# trust — run `just website-published` after changing it.
#
# Two files in this folder are deliberately NOT listed here: this file itself and
# `_headers`. The uploader reads both as configuration and reports "Ignoring
# asset" for each on its own, so listing them would be redundant — and listing
# `_headers` would additionally be a claim this repo has not verified, that the
# platform reads config after applying the ignore list rather than before.
#
/tools/demos/

# Note what is NOT here: `404.html` and `_headers` are configuration that ships,
# and `index.html`, `docs/index.html`, `assets/css/*`, `assets/js/main.js`, the
# player vendored beside it, the recorded take under `assets/cast/`,
# `assets/fonts/*`, `assets/img/terrain-matte.png`, `assets/img/og.png`, and
# `assets/img/speckle.svg` are the site itself.

# Authoring material
/.impeccable/
/tools/

# The gallery's corpus and the pipeline that builds it: the committed
# `poe.jsonl`, the Project Gutenberg cache beside it, and the two tools. `/tools/`
# above already excludes them; named here so the intent is declared rather than
# inherited, and asserted by published-tree.py. The built index is the exception:
# `assets/demo/` ships, because the browser searches it.
/PRODUCT.md
/README.md
/assets/img/terrain-v2.png
/assets/img/terrain-v2.md

# The sandbox service. `website/` is both the working tree and the publish
# source, and this is Go service code that happens to live here: its source,
# its server configuration, its preset Lua, its image build, and its terminal
# page must never be reachable at any path on the deployed origin. The whole
# directory is excluded, and `published-tree.py` asserts that it was — so a
# deleted line here fails the check rather than publishing the service.
/repl/

# The image plate's sample credits: an authoring note beside the images it
# describes, not a page. The images themselves ship (published-tree SERVED);
# this file does not.
/demos/samples/CREDITS.md
